/// mlrepro — the ANNOTATION CHECK does NOT ground a function's domain in a Map position: a pure-DOMAIN
/// arrow-annotation contradiction on a fn stored as a Map VALUE (or KEY) is NOT rejected. (corpus-hardening,
/// 2026-07-16, found by v-iterators — the annotation-check twin of the runtime-Map reflection leak)
///
/// This is the CHECK-side sibling of the reflect-side Map fn-domain leak v-inference just fixed (reflected_ty
/// Prim::MapInsert grounds key+value). The ANNOTATION CHECK (`(: expr T)`) grounds a fn's domain for the
/// tuple/list/record-element and sum-payload positions (07-type-system.sexp cases "a contradictory arrow
/// annotation on a function INSIDE a compound / in a SUM payload is rejected") — but NOT the Map position.
///
/// THE BUG: annotating a Map whose value function has a CONTRADICTORY DOMAIN is accepted. The check reads the
/// Map value fn's type bottom-up as `(-> Any Int64)` (domain left `Any`), so the annotated `Bool` domain
/// unifies with `Any` and the mismatch is masked:
///   def h(x) = x + 1                              // h : Int64 -> Int64
///   (Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, h) : Map(Int64, Bool -> Int64))   // pure-domain contradiction
///   → NOT rejected (only a CDZ0306 unused-def warning; check exit 0)
/// A CODOMAIN difference IS still caught (the codomain is concrete), which masked this at first — the domain
/// is the leak. CONTRAST (both correctly reject the same pure-domain contradiction, proving Map is the gap):
///   (Option.Some(h) : Option(Bool -> Int64))   → CDZ0203 "payload should be (-> Bool Int64), but ... (-> Int64 Int64)"
///   ((h, 0) : Tuple(Bool -> Int64, Int64))      → CDZ0203 "element 0 should be (-> Bool Int64), but ... (-> Int64 Int64)"
/// The KEY position leaks identically (a fn Map key compiles + runs, so its annotated domain should ground too).
///
/// OWNER: v-inference (the annotation-grounding seam, sibling of reflected_ty). Fix direction = ground a fn's
/// domain from its body in the Map value+key positions during the annotation check, exactly as the compound/
/// sum-payload annotation check already does (and matching the reflected_ty (Map k v) grounding fix).
///
/// EXPECTED (when fixed): the pure-domain Map value/key contradiction rejects CDZ0203, grounding the domain
/// to `(-> Int64 Int64)`. Then the annotation-check Map coverage cases (held) can land as (error CDZ0203).

def h(x) = x + 1

/// BUG: a pure-DOMAIN contradiction on a Map VALUE fn is NOT rejected (domain left Any). This @test expects
/// a compile-time REJECT; today it compiles (the annotation is wrongly accepted), so the program runs — the
/// test documents the gap (it should not reach a value at all once the check grounds the domain).
@test
def map-value-pure-domain-contradiction-should-reject() =
  let _m = (Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, h) : Map(Int64, Bool -> Int64)) in
  trap("BUG: pure-domain contradiction on a Map value fn was ACCEPTED (should reject CDZ0203)")

/// CONTROL: the sum-payload annotation check DOES ground the domain — this correctly rejects (so this @test
/// never runs; it is here to document the contrast, and would be a COMPILE error, which the harness records).
